Depending on your DRIVER you see the FOLLOWING:

Q -> TEXT is in Near LETTER Quality <-q
B -> TEXT is in BOLD <-b
I -> TEXT is in ITALIC <-i
U -> TEXT is UNDERLINED <-u
D -> TEXT is DOUBLE STRIKE <-d
W -> TEXT is in DOUBLE WIDE MODE <-w
IB-> TEXT is in ITALIC and BOLD <-bi
BW-> TEXT is in DOUBLE WIDE MODE AND BOLD <-wb

X -> TEXT in PICA/NORMAL style <-
Y -> TEXT in ELITE style <-
Z -> TEXT in CONDENSED style <-

